<article class="env-lemma" id="0G95">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G95">Lemma <span data-tag="0G95">15.72.6</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $I \subset R$ be an ideal. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to K \to P \to M \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> be a short exact sequence of $R$-modules. If $M$ is $I$-projective and $P$ is projective, then $K$ is $I$-projective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The element $\text{id}_ K \in \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(K, K)$ maps to the class of the given extension in $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ R(M, K)$. Since by assumption this class is annihilated by any $a \in I$ we see that $a : K \to K$ factors through $K \to P$ and we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>